{"name":"Barossa","hex":"#452e39","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Barossa","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A local government area in the Barossa Valley, South Australia; in full, Barossa Council."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Barossa"}],"entries":[{"title":"Barossa Valley","blocks":[{"text":"The Barossa Valley is a valley in South Australia located 60 kilometres (37 mi) northeast of Adelaide city centre. The valley is formed by the North Para River. It is notable as a major wine-producing region and tourist destination."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Tanunda.jpg/330px-Tanunda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barossa_Valley","wikidata":"Q698920"},{"title":"Electoral district of Barossa","blocks":[{"text":"Barossa was an electoral district of the House of Assembly in the colony of South Australia from 1857 to 1938 and again from 1956 to 1970. Barossa was also the name of an electoral district of the unicameral South Australian Legislative Council from 1851 until its abolition in 1857, George Fife Angas being the member."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electoral_district_of_Barossa","wikidata":"Q16962291"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Barossa_Valley_OSM.png/500px-Barossa_Valley_OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Barossa_Valley_OSM.png/1280px-Barossa_Valley_OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Barossa_Valley_OSM.png/500px-Barossa_Valley_OSM.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A detailed map of the Barossa Valley","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarossa_Valley_OSM.png